{{also|Tricolour}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|tricolor||US spelling}}

===Etymology===
An [[anglicisation]] of the {{der|en|fr|tricolore}}; the flag originated in France. Equivalent to {{prefix|en|tri|colour}}.
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtrɪkələ, -lɔː/|/ˈtraɪˌkʌlə/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtraɪˌkʌlɚ/|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

{{lb|en|UK spelling}}
# A [[flag]] consisting of three stripes that are either [[vertical]] or [[horizontal]]; all of equal size, and of a different colour each.
#: {{ux|en|'''Tricolours''' are seen in the national flags of over twenty [[countries]], including [[Belgium]], [[France]], [[India]], [[Italy]], [[Russia]], [[The Netherlands]] and the [[Republic of Ireland]].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Rory Carroll|title=‘Government is not listening’: anger over immigration spills into riot on Dublin’s streets|work=The Guardian|date=2023-11-24|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/nov/24/anger-immigration-riot-dublin-ireland|issn=0261-3077|passage=Journalists too were unwelcome and photographers had to conceal cameras. “He’s with the Guardian,” a man in his 60s, holding a '''tricolour''', shouted. }}

